WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.871
27 detectors to

00:00:01.683 --> 00:00:02.932
find network faults

00:00:02.744 --> 00:00:03.604
in seconds

00:00:04.134 --> 00:00:05.501
PcapAnalyzer is a

00:00:05.313 --> 00:00:07.023
free open-source tool

00:00:07.212 --> 00:00:08.261
upload a pcap

00:00:08.073 --> 00:00:08.815
capture

00:00:08.839 --> 00:00:09.617
and it tells

00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:09.994
you what is

00:00:09.806 --> 00:00:10.466
failing

00:00:10.526 --> 00:00:11.751
why and what

00:00:11.563 --> 00:00:12.518
to check next

00:00:13.054 --> 00:00:14.315
It runs 27

00:00:14.127 --> 00:00:15.495
detectors on every

00:00:15.306 --> 00:00:17.181
capture covering TCP

00:00:16.993 --> 00:00:18.289
retransmissions and

00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:19.386
firewall resets

00:00:19.528 --> 00:00:21.214
DNS and DHCP

00:00:21.026 --> 00:00:21.804
failures

00:00:21.875 --> 00:00:22.900
path problems

00:00:22.971 --> 00:00:24.138
TLS issues

00:00:24.245 --> 00:00:25.707
broken VPN tunnels

00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:26.768
and port scans

00:00:27.302 --> 00:00:28.021
It runs on

00:00:27.833 --> 00:00:28.776
your own machine

00:00:28.859 --> 00:00:30.108
so captures never

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:30.839
leave your network

00:00:30.981 --> 00:00:31.676
and it is

00:00:31.488 --> 00:00:32.585
currently in beta

00:00:32.396 --> 00:00:33.469
under the Apache

00:00:33.281 --> 00:00:34.896
2.0 license

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.444
Full story on

00:00:36.255 --> 00:00:37.151
the dashboard
